  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Right-hand controller unable to trigger when VRChat window loses focus until the Quick Menu is opened again\nSteps to reproduce:\n- Video: https://vrcdn.video/hai/57a08ac476234bdaf9d6ac5281467392.mp4\n- Press the right controller trigger on an interact: The interact functions\n- Open the SteamVR desktop view, or open XSOverlay, or open OVR Toolkit\n- On the desktop view, click on any other window that is not VRChat (do NOT minimize the VRChat window)\n- Close the desktop view\n- Press the right controller trigger on an interact\nObserved (independently):\n- Pressing the right-hand controller trigger on an interact does NOT trigger\n- Pressing the left-hand controller trigger on an interact does trigger correctly\nAdditional notes:\n- Opening the Desktop view, focusing the VRChat window, and closing the Desktop view, then pressing the right-hand controller trigger on an interact does trigger\n- Opening the quick menu, closing it, then pressing the right-hand controller trigger on an interact does trigger\n- Opening the right-hand Action Menu Wheel, then opening the left-hand quick menu, then closing the left-hand quick menu with the left-hand quick menu button, then pressing the right-hand controller trigger on an interact does NOT trigger\nExpected:\n- The interact should function\n-----\nNote: This report is different from \"https://feedback.vrchat.com/bug-reports/p/ui-interactionpickups-cant-be-interacted-with-if-vrchat-window-not-focused\" because in my case, the right controller trigger continues to function even when the VRChat window is minimized out of focus.",
